# SwarmCompile Phase 1, slice 1 of 2 (prototype -- see
# self_hosting/swarm_compile/phase1_demo.patlang for the end-to-end
# proof and self_hosting/swarm_compile/job_queue.patlang for the
# claim/validate/commit states built on top of this).
#
# PURPOSE: wrap the ALREADY-WORKING, UNCHANGED per-function
# CompileUnit -> ChunkImage step (self_hosting/lib/x64_compile_unit.
# patlang's own CompileUnit class and ensure_chunk_native method) in an
# explicit, inspectable identity/provenance envelope -- a "SwarmArtefact"
# -- so a job queue (or, eventually, a distributed worker) can reason
# about WHAT a produced value is and WHERE it came from without
# re-deriving that from the ChunkImage's own opaque byte/symbol tables.
#
# This file does NOT change what gets computed. It does not touch
# ensure_chunk_native, emit_program_x64, x64_assemble_chunk, or any
# other codegen/assembly logic -- it only names, after the fact, the
# identity that logic already deterministically produces.
#
# NAMING NOTE (explicitly required by the governing spec): "SwarmArtefact"
# names a COMPILER-WORK product -- which worker/stage is allowed to
# transform a compilation artefact (this function's IR, its ChunkImage).
# It is NEVER used for, and must never be confused with, PatLang's own
# runtime value ownership (Box/refcounting semantics a COMPILED PROGRAM
# manipulates, e.g. general-refcounting.md's bm_rc_inc/bm_rc_dec). Those
# are a completely different kind of "ownership," at a different level
# (the compiler's own bookkeeping vs. the compiled program's own
# runtime heap), and this module's vocabulary (artefact/job/claim/
# validate/commit) is kept out of self_hosting/block_model/lower.patlang,
# self_hosting/lib/codegen_x64.patlang, and self_hosting/lib/
# x64_runtime.patlang entirely, on purpose, so the two can never be
# textually confused by a future reader grepping for "owner".
#
# Representation: a plain tagged list, same convention as ChunkImage/
# FuncIR/ProgramIR elsewhere in this codebase (["ChunkImage", ...],
# ["FuncIR", ...]) rather than a new class -- this is supporting
# vocabulary for print/inspect/compare, not a new runtime mechanism.
#
#   ["SwarmArtefact",
#     artefact_id,       -- stable string, derived ONLY from kind +
#                           content_hash (see below) -- never from
#                           worker identity, claim order, or wall time.
#     content_hash,       -- CompileUnit's own content_hash: a hash of
#                           this function's canonical JSON-serialized
#                           IR, folded with x64_compiler_fingerprint()
#                           (a hash of codegen_x64.patlang's own
#                           source -- see x64_compile_unit.patlang's
#                           own header for why: so a codegen change
#                           invalidates identity even when the
#                           function's own IR did not change). This
#                           already satisfies the "stable identifiers
#                           from canonical content + declared
#                           compilation context" rule on its own --
#                           this module does not recompute or
#                           reinterpret it, only carries it forward.
#     producer,            -- the exact function that computed the
#                           payload (a plain string, so a human or a
#                           future validator can tell what produced
#                           this without re-deriving it): always
#                           "x64_compile_unit.ensure_chunk_native" for
#                           this slice.
#     dep_names,           -- the FULL, EXPLICIT extern-name list this
#                           unit's own codegen was given (x64_
#                           extern_names_for's return value) -- i.e.
#                           every OTHER symbol this function's own
#                           compiled body is allowed to reference.
#                           This is the job's own declared dependency
#                           contract: nothing outside this list may be
#                           consulted by the transformation that
#                           produced this artefact's payload.
#     kind,                -- "ChunkImage" for this slice (the one
#                           stage being wrapped). A string, not an
#                           enum, so a later slice can add a new kind
#                           (e.g. "ParsedAst", "LoweredIR") without
#                           changing this shape.
#     payload]             -- the ChunkImage itself (or, on failure,
#                           an "ASM ERROR:"-prefixed string -- the
#                           SAME failure convention ensure_chunk_native
#                           already uses, carried through unchanged).
#
# Deliberately NOT included: a timestamp, a worker id, a sequence
# number. Per the governing rule ("stable identifiers derived from
# canonical content... never worker order or completion timing"), none
# of those may be part of identity, so none are stored as if they were.

include "../lib/x64_compile_unit.patlang"

# swarm_artefact_id(kind, content_hash) -> the stable id string.
# Pulled out as its own function (rather than inlined at each call
# site) so "how an id is built from a hash" has exactly one definition
# -- any later artefact kind reuses this unchanged.
make a function called swarm_artefact_id takes kind, content_hash returns id
  return "artefact:" + kind + ":" + content_hash
end

# swarm_make_chunk_artefact(unit, extern_names, chunk_or_err) -> a
# SwarmArtefact wrapping whatever ensure_chunk_native already returned
# for this CompileUnit. Takes the CompileUnit and the SAME extern_names
# list that was passed into ensure_chunk_native, so dep_names reflects
# the job's own true declared contract rather than being re-derived or
# guessed after the fact.
make a function called swarm_make_chunk_artefact takes unit, extern_names, chunk_or_err returns artefact
  let content_hash = get(unit, "content_hash")
  let aid = swarm_artefact_id("ChunkImage", content_hash)
  return ["SwarmArtefact", aid, content_hash, "x64_compile_unit.ensure_chunk_native", extern_names, "ChunkImage", chunk_or_err]
end

# ---- field accessors (plain index reads, named so call sites don't
# hard-code the tuple's own shape). ----
make a function called swarm_artefact_id_of takes artefact returns id
  return artefact[1]
end

make a function called swarm_artefact_content_hash takes artefact returns h
  return artefact[2]
end

make a function called swarm_artefact_producer takes artefact returns p
  return artefact[3]
end

make a function called swarm_artefact_dep_names takes artefact returns names
  return artefact[4]
end

make a function called swarm_artefact_kind takes artefact returns k
  return artefact[5]
end

make a function called swarm_artefact_payload takes artefact returns payload
  return artefact[6]
end

# swarm_artefact_failed(artefact) -> true if the payload is the
# "ASM ERROR:"-prefixed failure string ensure_chunk_native uses,
# rather than a real ChunkImage. Checked via type_of (a ChunkImage is
# a list; an error is a string) -- same discriminator x64_compile_
# unit.patlang's own X64UnitLinker.build_native already uses for this
# exact distinction, kept consistent rather than reinvented.
make a function called swarm_artefact_failed takes artefact returns failed
  let payload = swarm_artefact_payload(artefact)
  return type_of(payload) == "string"
end
